# Project Rules

## Core Rules

- Follow all project rules before generating or modifying code.
- If project rules conflict, architecture rules have the highest priority.
- Do not introduce new libraries, frameworks, build tools, state managers or project dependencies unless explicitly requested by the user.
- Do not replace existing architectural patterns with alternative approaches unless explicitly requested.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless the user explicitly requests breaking changes.
- When architecture changes (new modules, layers, services, public APIs, project structure or interaction flow), update the project README accordingly.
- When requirements are ambiguous, prefer consistency with existing project architecture over introducing a new approach.
